## What changed

- A1/DE1: 22.8 GB is `tc_names.oo` + `token_fmt.oo` O(n²) char-concat, linear O(np), ~150 MB/module.
- A2/DE2: 159:27 → `c_emit_struct.oo:158` needs `let mut ok`.
- A3/RT: C-side leaks in `arity_get`/`scan_has_name`/`drop_depth` amplify by ~100×.
- A4/PV1: `p7_check_main_smoke.oo` does NOT check RSS or build ID; multiple non-124 codes ALL OK.
- A5/PV2: closure reproducible 3/3; 1/3 SIGKILL environmental, not compiler.
- A6/SEC: token-count cap missing; 1-line repro documented.
- A7/MEM: linear 699 MiB/s, unbounded — would OOM at higher `np`.
- A8/INT: fresh ELF reproduces; closure is not a stale-ELF accident.
- A9/HARN: `harness_f26_residual_smoke.oo` at `ooda/scripts/` (61 lines; unbuilt; build blocked by SPRINT Task 8).
- A10/HYG: 5 runtime `.c` files >256 lines; 5 live `.tmp.c` sludge.
- A11/DOCS: `openOODA/audit/f26_residual.oot` (36 lines).

